From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi: follow the v6.16 rename of from_timer()

v6.16 replaced from_timer() with timer_container_of() and removed the old
name. BUILD_TIMER_FUNCTION() expands to a timer callback that is emitted into
every translation unit including rt_linux.h, so the whole driver failed with
"implicit declaration of function 'from_timer'" as soon as the first object
was built. Alias the helper once and keep the 4.19+ branch unchanged.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt_wifi/include/os/rt_linux.h
+++ b/mt_wifi/include/os/rt_linux.h
@@ -487,11 +487,22 @@
 typedef void (*TIMER_FUNCTION)(unsigned long);
 #endif
 
+/*
+ * v6.16 renamed from_timer() to timer_container_of(); the old name is gone and
+ * the timer callback below is expanded in every translation unit that includes
+ * this header, so the alias has to be resolved before BUILD_TIMER_FUNCTION().
+ */
+#if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 16, 0))
+#define MT_FROM_TIMER(_ptr, _timer, _field)	timer_container_of(_ptr, _timer, _field)
+#else
+#define MT_FROM_TIMER(_ptr, _timer, _field)	from_timer(_ptr, _timer, _field)
+#endif
+
 #if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(4,19,0))
 #define BUILD_TIMER_FUNCTION(_func) \
 void rtmp_timer_##_func(struct timer_list *_timer) \
 { \
-	PRALINK_TIMER_STRUCT	pTimer = from_timer(pTimer,_timer,TimerObj); \
+	PRALINK_TIMER_STRUCT	pTimer = MT_FROM_TIMER(pTimer,_timer,TimerObj); \
  \
 	_func(NULL, (PVOID) pTimer->cookie, NULL, pTimer); \
 	if (pTimer->Repeat) \
